#pragma once
// Generated by tools/gen_app_info.py - edit the data there. Drives the Changelog, Info and Mod support menus.
#include <vector>

struct ChangelogEntry {const char* version;const char* date;const char* title;std::vector<const char*> items;};
struct SupportRow {const char* name;const char* status;};
struct SupportGroup {const char* title;std::vector<SupportRow> rows;};

inline constexpr const char* appVersion="1.10";

inline constexpr const char* appEdition=" (shareable edition)";
inline const std::vector<ChangelogEntry>& appChangelog(){static const std::vector<ChangelogEntry> data={
    {"1.10","27 Oct 2026","Claude: surface blocks as the game makes them (nothing simplified)",{"The cursor readout, clicks, points and markers now use the terrain exactly as drawn (full resolution, the finer patch and ring included); before they read a coarse 129 x 129 sample and could miss by over 100 blocks on large worlds. Not included: river and lake water surfaces in the FTF land view (the readout gives the river bed there).","New Copy coordinates tool [K] in the viewport toolbar: click the terrain to copy X Y Z of that spot (block coordinates, Y on top of the ground, ready after /tp).","Ctrl+Shift+right-drag in the viewport turns the sun around (like rotating the HDRI in Substance Painter); the height stays.","Find highest point replaces its old marker instead of adding another, the marker sits on the drawn terrain, and the search reads the terrain in small bands (no single 1 GB copy at the 8192 size).","New Biomes generated section (right panel): Count biomes scans the whole preview world (512 / 1024 / 2048 samples) and shows how many of the biomes your settings can produce actually appear, per mod, with the list of the ones that did not and the ones no climate table in use can select. Use it to size a world so every biome generates.","Surface blocks now follow Minecraft 1.21.1 and FTF exactly, block by block at the chosen resolution: Minecraft's own seeded noises, surface depth, temperature, the preliminary surface and the vertical gradients, checked bit for bit against the game's classes.","FTF strata (the soil, sediment, clay and rock layers per region) are now the real FTF stacks for the world seed, so cliffs and scree show the same rock bands as in the game.","Snow follows the game: snow layers where it is cold enough, FTF's snow erosion on steep slopes and its smoothed layers (full snow blocks where the layers add up).","River water as FTF places it: wetlands and river stretches fill to their own water level (upland marshes used to sit about 62 blocks too low), with the stone fills along banks and valley floors.","Steep terrain now has the same heights as the real world: FTF's cliff and erosion filters sample their noise 32 blocks off (the tile border), and the app now does the same. Exact heights on steep snowy badlands went from 23% to 96% of columns.","Adaptive finer detail is faster and smooth: the biome and block pass (about 90% of a build) is 25-39% faster with identical blocks, and the background patch builds in small slices, so the two ~1 second freezes per zoom are gone.","Fixed adaptive finer detail disappearing whenever the camera moved (orbit and fly): moving used to throw the finished patch away and restart its build after you stopped. The last patch now stays on screen while you move and a build in progress keeps going. Background builds also fit more work per frame (about 1.7 s for a patch and ring at 60 fps in tests, was about 4 s).","Dragging a slider with adaptive finer detail on now rebuilds the close patch and its ring first, at full detail with the newest values (about every 1-2 s while you drag), and only then refines the rest of the world. The old behaviours stay as choices under \"While dragging a slider\" in the camera LOD settings.","New Settings menu: lock the viewport frame rate (20-240 fps or off, 60 by default; the time left in each frame goes to building terrain) and reset all app settings (view, quality, LOD bands, finer detail, atmosphere, trees, camera, panels), with a confirmation. Presets, projects, the library, points and recent files are kept.","Faster surface blocks with identical results: each column now computes only the Minecraft noises its biome can read. The biome and block pass is about 42% faster, and a finer-detail patch builds in about a third of the frames.","New Info menu: what the preview matches exactly, what is an approximation and what is not shown.","Undo, redo, save and open shortcuts (Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y or Ctrl+Shift+Z, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+O) now also work in walk (Minecraft) and fly (Unreal) navigation.","Consistent interface: one header style with the icons inside the bars, every label above its control, one value style (slider plus a number box to type in), the same units everywhere (60°, 1.00x, 1500 blocks), sentence-case names, one checkbox per line, no duplicate text or Undo/Redo buttons. The Biome finder is on the toolbar only, with its own shortcut N."}},
    {"1.9","26 Oct 2026","Claude: finer-detail holes, live finer preview, 2D clouds, trees, lakes",{"Fixed two causes of a sky-coloured hole before finer detail fills in: the intermediate ring cut its hole where the new patch will be (not where the last complete one is drawn), and the whole-world grid assumed a ring twice the patch size (wrong with the ring-width slider).","Finer detail while dragging sliders: choose the preview size (256 / 512 / 1024 / 2048, default 512), or turn on \"Full finer detail while dragging\" for full detail on every change (can lag).","Clouds are now a flat 2D layer (cloud height, size, coverage, density, opacity, wind); the volumetric clouds are removed.","Trees: when a view holds more trees than a tree list fits, they are now thinned evenly (a counting pass first) instead of whole areas going missing. Trees in the intermediate ring now sit on the ring's finer surface (they used the coarse grid there and could be buried or float).","Lake highlight: lakes made by widening rivers are marked as lakes (rivers no longer include them), and inland ground below sea level counts as lake. Basins FTF itself classifies as shallow ocean are not separated from the sea yet."}},
    {"1.8.1","26 Oct 2026","Claude: walk crash fix, obsolete controls removed",{"Fixed a crash in walk mode with a large finer-detail patch (for example patch radius 4000+ or finest spacing 4 blocks): the intermediate ring was swapped in before it had ever been set up. Replaying the crashing session: 8 of 8 walks now finish (all crashed before).","A crash now writes its call stack to state/crash-log.txt.","Removed obsolete controls: the duplicate walk FOV (one FOV stays in View / scene), the old pre-FTF Surface and Climate colour sliders, the hand-placed High detail tool (adaptive finer detail replaces it; an old placed patch is dropped on load) and the Animate / stress test. Every FTF preset slider stays."}},
    {"1.8","26 Oct 2026","Claude: queue 5 (walk, bands, finer detail, trees, heights, shareable edition)",{"Two editions: the normal one, and a shareable one (FTF + vanilla Minecraft only, no biome-mod data or names, FTF default presets only).","Walk mode: choose the walk tool, then click anywhere on the terrain to spawn there. Leaving walk turns the orbit camera to look at where you stood. Walk settings are always visible, and one FOV is shared by orbit, fly and walk.","The 1-block terrain patch under the walker is removed; walking uses the finer-detail heights (small windows around the player: worst frame while streaming 362 -> 36 ms in tests).","Six-band LOD: number of bands (1-8), each band's width and detail are adjustable. Adaptive finer detail: patch radius and ring width sliders.","Adaptive finer detail now works in orbit, fly and walk, no longer turns off while values change, and builds the full patch in the background (slider drag at 2048: typical frame 2.6 ms; full-patch rebuild stall 192 -> 39 ms).","Preset values update live while dragging; new \"Apply on release\" toggle.","Dropdowns for continent shape, spawn type, every FTF noise type and biome search quality.","Height tools: the overflow highlight now marks terrain FTF squeezes under the world ceiling; highlight everything above a chosen Y; find the highest point (adds a map point).","Trees use the same frustum and distance culling as the terrain (the fixed cone dropped trees at screen sides), and can hide while the camera moves (toggle, saved).","Terrain cloud shadows are saved with projects again."}},
    {"1.7","26 Oct 2026","Claude: detail ring order, walk fixes, finer-detail bar",{"Adaptive finer detail is now always ordered near patch > intermediate ring > six bands: the ring uses the full patch grid over twice the width (twice the patch spacing instead of four times) and is no longer coarsened by distance (its outer edge used to drop below the whole-world grid). Example at 64k / 1024: patch 8.0, ring 16.1, base 64.1 blocks per sample.","New loading bar along the bottom of the 3D viewport for adaptive finer detail: waiting for the camera to stop, settling, generating (and waiting for the map while it refines).","New \"Finer detail in walk and fly modes\" checkbox (six-band LOD menu, on by default, saved with the view): off keeps only the whole-world grid in Minecraft and Unreal navigation.","Walk mode: the player is a 0.6 x 0.6 block column standing on the highest ground under it, so the view no longer sinks into rising slopes; movement is split into 0.1-block substeps so steps up to 0.6 block are climbed at any frame rate (higher ledges need a jump).","Walk-mode water and sky flicker: the atmosphere pass now works camera-relative and takes distance from linear depth (the walk near/far ratio of 1:16 million made the old reconstruction noisy), and water ripples smaller than a pixel fade out instead of shimmering as you move."}},
    {"1.6","26 Oct 2026","Claude: much faster slider edits, collapsed panels",{"Terrain regeneration is about 5x faster with identical results: a full 2048 x 2048 update went from 588 ms to 116 ms of GPU time (rivers 415 ms -> 14 ms, erosion filter 68 ms -> 4 ms). The FTF sine lookup table now lives in a GPU buffer instead of a constant array that the GPU copied into slow memory on every lookup, and river branches that cannot reach a point are skipped.","The full-resolution map arrives much sooner after you release a slider: background refinement now does as many whole steps per frame as the time budget allows (2048: about 0.15 s after the settle delay instead of several seconds; 4096: about 0.5 s).","Closing the app no longer hangs for about 14 seconds after background refinement (a GPU driver slowdown with tiled dispatches).","All panel sections start collapsed when the app opens."}},
    {"1.5","26 Oct 2026","Claude: performance, realistic water, volumetric fog and clouds",{"Walk mode no longer freezes while the terrain around you streams: collision heights are read back asynchronously (worst-case frames 90 ms -> 1.7 ms in the walk-streaming test).","New \"Atmosphere (display only)\" section in View / scene with three independent toggles, all off by default and saved with your graphics settings.","Realistic water: animated ripples, Fresnel sky reflection, sun glint, depth absorption and shore foam on the sea.","Volumetric fog: height fog that is thickest over the sea and in valleys, tinted by the sky and sun (density, height falloff, base height).","Volumetric clouds: a drifting, self-shadowed cloud layer ray-marched between two heights (coverage, density, base height, thickness, size, wind speed).","With Responsive editing preview off, grids above 1024 no longer regenerate in one long GPU job (about 0.6 s per change at 2048 and 2.4 s at 4096, which could trip the Windows GPU watchdog and crash): the last map stays on screen and the new one is refined in small background jobs, with the loading bar.","Fog and clouds have an Opacity slider each; turning volumetric clouds on switches the old terrain / cloud shadows off (and locks that checkbox).","With any atmosphere option on, the flat background becomes a sky; with all three off the image is identical to before (the extra pass costs about 0.02 ms).","Performance report now lists stall timers (walk heights, rivers, picking, hover) so slow frames can be traced."}},
    {"1.4","26 Oct 2026","Claude: loading bar, 1024 preview, high-camera fix, view-focused trees, colour coding",{"A loading bar under the viewport status shows how far the responsive viewport has come toward the full selected resolution.","Responsive editing quality gained a 1024 x 1024 option (256 / 512 / 1024).","The teal ring overlay around the high-detail patch is gone.","The intermediate detail ring is only used where it is finer than the terrain around it (it used to look coarser than its surroundings at some zoom levels).","Adaptive finer detail has an \"Apply only after the camera stops\" toggle (on by default): it is hidden while you move and returns a moment after you stop, like the trees.","Six-band LOD is altitude-aware: bands use 3D distance and widen with camera height, so a very high camera keeps full detail (about one eighth of the triangles of no LOD) instead of blurring the whole map.","Entire-map overview trees follow the view: the window is centred on what you look at, cells behind the camera are skipped, and vanilla tree kinds have 8x larger instance segments, so forests fill in.","Panels and sections are colour coded (green surface controls, blue viewport, violet view and quality, amber project actions; sections by terrain, climate/biome, rivers, islands, erosion/surface, world, walk/points).","New Changelog and Mod support menus next to File."}},
    {"1.3","26 Oct 2026","ChatGPT: updates",{"Responsive editing preview (A): preview updates while dragging, then refinement to the selected Grid in small GPU jobs with cancellation and promotion.","Selective stage updates (C): terrain, climate, filter, biome-only and material-only changes reuse cached stages.","Automatic intermediate near-detail ring, FOV and culling options, one client-drawn window caption, query-frame fixes after swapchain changes."}},
    {"1.2","26 Oct 2026","Claude: versions, trees, walk, fly, points, adaptive LOD",{"FTF version selector: 1.0.0014 (default), 1.0.0013, 1.0.0010; per-version erosion constants, table trigonometry and terrain ceiling before rivers, verified against the 1.0.0013 filter classes.","Blocky Minecraft-style trees of 12 kinds placed per biome with vanilla densities, toggle with settings dropdown, hidden while settings change.","Walk mode (Minecraft-like movement, 1-block terrain patch, 1/16-block grid), Unreal-style fly camera, Esc leaves both.","Per-project Points with a right-panel list, player icon at the spawn point, fullscreen start with F11.","Six-band LOD became a viewport view with adaptive resolution (finer while zooming, minimum and maximum resolution).","Animate settings sweeps twelve real settings on a copy of the preset and restores everything exactly.","Faster start-up: parallel and on-demand pipeline compilation, loading screen and persisted pipeline cache (cold 109 s to 26 s, warm 0.5 s).","Stable FTF 1.0.0 support was removed."}},
    {"1.1","26 Oct 2026","ChatGPT: editor tools, lighting, inspector, projects",{"Clickable preset history, reset to last saved state, Save as new preset, docked panels with corner hide buttons.","Biome finder, six-band geometry LOD, world-radius high-detail brush (H), spawn, centre and measure tools.","Adjustable sun with terrain shadows, ambient occlusion and cloud shadows, terrain hover inspector (biome, terrain, block, height).","Projects with autosave and crash recovery, per-preset preview extent, reset camera."}},
    {"1.0","25 Oct 2026","ChatGPT: full FTF surface",{"Native Vulkan surface preview with all four continent types, archipelagos, rivers, lakes, wetlands, FTF climate, Minecraft biome selection and world filters (Phacelle erosion with cliff relaxation).","Minecraft block colours with biome tints and FTF scree, preset library with datapack import and export."}},
    {"0.9","24 Oct 2026","ChatGPT: first viewer",{"Native Vulkan viewer, FTF noise primitives and the first isolated terrain graphs."}},
};return data;}
inline const std::vector<SupportGroup>& appInfo(){static const std::vector<SupportGroup> data={
    {"Exact: matches the game at every sample",{{"Terrain height (FTF 1.0.0010)","FTF's own terrain graphs, continents, mountains, volcanoes, rivers, lakes, wetlands, climate and world filters, ported and checked against FTF's code. Against a real world from the same seed and preset, 94-99% of columns have the exact height in the test areas."},{"Terrain height (FTF 1.0.0013 / 1.0.0014)","The same port with those versions' filter settings; not yet compared with a real world."},{"Biomes","Minecraft 1.21.1's own biome table and lookup on FTF's climate values (shown per sample, without the game's 4-block biome blending)."},{"Surface blocks (vanilla)","Minecraft 1.21.1's surface rules with its seeded noises, surface depth, temperature and preliminary surface, plus FTF's strata, scree, snow and river water. Checked bit for bit against the game's own classes."}}},
    {"Approximate",{{"Trees","Kinds follow each biome's tree features; positions and shapes are approximations (not seed-exact)."},{"Colours","One representative colour per block, with the biome's grass, foliage and water tints."},{"Resolution","Each sample is one exact block column; the mesh between samples is interpolated. A coarser grid is the same terrain shown at lower resolution, not a simplified one."}}},
    {"Not shown",{{"Underground and other dimensions","Caves, ores below the surface, the Nether and the End."},{"Structures and small features","Villages and other structures, flowers, grass, boulders and other decorations (except those listed above)."},{"FTF 1.0.0 (stable)","Not supported (its droplet erosion cannot be reproduced)."}}},
};return data;}
